# Post-call self-healing

When a voice call ends (a `spark-voice` hang-up: the relay says the call ended, or delivers what the user said on the call), run the `sparks-postcall` procedure in full before moving on to other work.

`sparks-postcall` sets `disable-model-invocation`, so the model will not invoke it on its own. Open the plugin's `skills/sparks-postcall/SKILL.md` and follow it from start to finish. If you cannot open that file, ask the user to run `/sparks-postcall`.

The post-call protocol lives only in `sparks-postcall`, not in `spark-voice`. `spark-voice` stops at hang-up and hands over the transcript paths; it does not extract the spec, verify the call's work, implement gaps, or merge PRs. That self-healing loop is `sparks-postcall`.
